WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.842
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.112 --> 00:09.114
[theme music playing]

3
00:35.724 --> 00:37.726
[intense music playing]

4
00:57.204 --> 00:58.372
[Song-yi] Hey.

5
00:59.331 --> 01:00.749
Hey, wait. Hold on.

6
01:02.334 --> 01:04.336
The boarding gates are that way.

7
01:20.519 --> 01:21.687
I'm in.

8
01:22.646 --> 01:24.690
What? [stammers] What do you…

9
01:24.773 --> 01:26.108
Let's do it.

10
01:27.109 --> 01:29.612
The Table: K-Chef 2026.

11
01:38.162 --> 01:41.206
[Woo-jin] The days when chefs just stayed in the kitchen are over.

12
01:41.290 --> 01:44.668
Of course, we can't leave the kitchen behind.

13
01:45.169 --> 01:48.547
[chuckles] What matters is working to put

14
01:48.631 --> 01:51.342
development and business on the same scale

15
01:51.926 --> 01:53.218
and finding the right balance.

16
01:53.886 --> 01:56.597
Korean dining can't grow without economies of scale.

17
01:57.306 --> 01:58.557
Exactly.

18
01:58.641 --> 02:02.061
Like you said, if an industry isn't backed by solid business,

19
02:02.144 --> 02:05.189
it ends up becoming just another exclusive playground

20
02:05.272 --> 02:07.107
for a handful of gourmets.

21
02:07.191 --> 02:10.069
Even with K-food gaining global attention,

22
02:10.152 --> 02:14.031
some pessimists point out the trend is too focused on casual street food

23
02:14.114 --> 02:15.783
and will eventually run out of steam.

24
02:15.866 --> 02:17.952
This might pose a problem for us.

25
02:18.035 --> 02:19.036
That's right.

26
02:19.119 --> 02:20.412
Given this reality,

27
02:20.496 --> 02:24.458
what kind of effort do you think our industry realistically needs to make?

28
02:26.377 --> 02:28.754
I'd like to hear your personal thoughts on that, Chef.

29
02:31.465 --> 02:32.883
[chuckles]

30
02:32.967 --> 02:34.593
That's a tough question.

31
02:36.553 --> 02:37.888
Efforts that we

32
02:39.139 --> 02:40.975
realistically need to make…

33
02:43.227 --> 02:44.311
Oh…

34
02:47.815 --> 02:50.693
Word in the kitchen is that Pyeongyeon Group is planning

35
02:50.776 --> 02:55.155
a very interesting new TV show called The Table: K-Chef 2026.

36
02:55.948 --> 02:58.951
A competition to find the best Korean chef in the world.

37
02:59.034 --> 03:00.744
Sounds interesting, right?

38
03:01.328 --> 03:05.249
Surely you and Exception will also be participating in the competition, right?

39
03:05.332 --> 03:06.333
I'm not sure.

40
03:09.420 --> 03:11.046
Do you think it's a good idea?

41
03:13.048 --> 03:14.049
Do you…

42
03:16.510 --> 03:18.512
want me to enter the competition?

43
03:26.395 --> 03:27.479
Uh…

44
03:28.605 --> 03:30.441
Enter a cooking competition?

45
03:32.276 --> 03:33.318
Really? Us?

46
03:34.194 --> 03:35.738
Yes, Auntie.

47
03:37.489 --> 03:38.824
[whimsical music playing]

48
03:42.995 --> 03:44.288
I'm very excited.

49
03:45.789 --> 03:46.832
Oh…

50
03:49.918 --> 03:52.087
Uh… [gasps]

51
03:52.921 --> 03:53.922
[chuckles]

52
03:57.760 --> 03:58.761
[lock chimes]

53
03:58.844 --> 04:00.429
[phone buzzes]

54
04:03.348 --> 04:05.059
FAMIGLIA OWNER CHOI SONG-YI

55
04:05.142 --> 04:07.478
[Song-yi] Chris K. agreed to join us.

56
04:07.561 --> 04:09.772
Famiglia will enter the competition.

57
04:13.192 --> 04:14.234
[chuckles]

58
04:17.446 --> 04:19.490
[announcer] The Table: K-Chef 2026

59
04:19.573 --> 04:22.201
isn't looking for Korea's best restaurant or best dish.

60
04:22.284 --> 04:24.703
It's looking for Korea's best chef.

61
04:24.787 --> 04:26.622
It's not just about making delicious food.

62
04:26.705 --> 04:28.582
It's a culinary survival competition

63
04:28.665 --> 04:31.085
where creativity, challenge interpretation ability,

64
04:31.168 --> 04:33.796
artistry and more are comprehensively evaluated.

65
04:33.879 --> 04:35.089
To qualify for the competition,

66
04:35.172 --> 04:38.842
each four-member team must be led by an actively working Korean head chef.

67
04:38.926 --> 04:41.220
You'll create a dish that meets the challenge guidelines

68
04:41.303 --> 04:43.597
using a limited selection of ingredients, then you must present it…

69
04:43.680 --> 04:47.184
So far, it doesn't sound much different from any other cooking competition.

70
04:47.810 --> 04:50.270
No, this only covers the preliminary round.

71
04:50.354 --> 04:52.439
Listen to what he's going to say next.

72
04:52.523 --> 04:56.318
First, we'll give you a theme that will serve as the key word for the competition.

73
04:56.401 --> 04:59.238
You'll use that theme to prepare for the main round.

74
05:01.031 --> 05:04.201
One week later, at the studio where the main round will take place,

75
05:04.284 --> 05:07.913
we'll give you a specific cooking challenge related to that specific theme.

76
05:07.996 --> 05:10.415
Then each team will have three hours

77
05:10.499 --> 05:12.835
to discuss, cook and finish their dish.

78
05:13.377 --> 05:15.087
After serving the dish to the judges,

79
05:15.170 --> 05:18.465
each team's head chef will give a presentation for their dish.

80
05:18.549 --> 05:21.927
The highest score will go to the dish that best demonstrates an understanding

81
05:22.010 --> 05:24.304
of the deeper meaning behind the theme and challenge,

82
05:24.388 --> 05:26.431
or interprets them most creatively.

83
05:26.515 --> 05:30.352
Of course, what matters the most is the taste.

84
05:30.435 --> 05:32.437
A little tough, huh? [laughs]

85
05:32.521 --> 05:34.565
Just a little? It's insanely tough.

86
05:36.108 --> 05:38.694
-They could at least give us an example. -I'm afraid I can't help you guys.

87
05:38.777 --> 05:41.238
This is what sets this competition apart from all others,

88
05:41.321 --> 05:43.782
so I can't give you any examples. [chuckles]

89
05:43.866 --> 05:46.034
The key is to anticipate and understand

90
05:46.118 --> 05:48.745
the relationship between the theme and the challenge.

91
05:48.829 --> 05:50.873
That's why the one-week preparation period

92
05:50.956 --> 05:52.916
after the theme is announced will be crucial.

93
05:53.000 --> 05:55.127
One more thing. When I say the head chef must be Korean,

94
05:55.210 --> 05:57.421
I mean heritage, not nationality.

95
05:57.504 --> 06:01.008
As long as either parent is Korean, you're eligible to qualify.

96
06:01.091 --> 06:02.676
All right, everyone. Good luck!

97
06:02.759 --> 06:04.469
I hope to see you all in the main round.

98
06:04.553 --> 06:07.055
I, Captain Cook, will be honing my skills

99
06:07.139 --> 06:09.725
and doing my best to make it to the main round too.

100
06:12.060 --> 06:14.021
[Du-yeong laughing]

101
06:14.897 --> 06:16.356
I've watched this over and over,

102
06:16.440 --> 06:18.734
and I still have no idea what he's talking about.

103
06:18.817 --> 06:21.069
So they're going to give us a theme,

104
06:21.153 --> 06:24.865
then they're going to give us a challenge about that theme a week later?

105
06:24.948 --> 06:26.700
What does it mean? [inhales sharply]

106
06:26.783 --> 06:29.244
Couldn't they at least give an example?

107
06:29.328 --> 06:31.246
What kind of competition is this?

108
06:31.330 --> 06:33.165
Do you think we should call some other chefs?

109
06:33.248 --> 06:35.834
Someone must've understood all that gibberish he said.

110
06:37.461 --> 06:41.089
[sighs] I bet Pyeongyeon gave some hints to chefs they're close to.

111
06:42.090 --> 06:43.091
Listen.

112
06:44.051 --> 06:46.386
Don't we need to pass the preliminary round

113
06:46.470 --> 06:49.306
before we worry about what any of that means, huh?

114
06:50.098 --> 06:53.852
Let's focus on how we're gonna pass the preliminary round first, yeah?

115
06:54.353 --> 06:58.148
Okay. The requirement is a four-member team.

116
06:59.983 --> 07:02.027
But we're only two.

117
07:05.656 --> 07:06.865
Uh, right…

118
07:07.616 --> 07:08.617
Just two.

119
07:09.743 --> 07:10.953
[sighs]

120
07:14.414 --> 07:15.624
[sighs]

121
07:15.707 --> 07:17.626
Can we even find someone else?

122
07:18.752 --> 07:22.172
It's been a few months since we posted the kitchen staff listing.

123
07:24.049 --> 07:27.344
Unless someone's dying to get on Pyeongyeon Group's bad side…

124
07:27.427 --> 07:28.595
[clicks tongue]

125
07:28.679 --> 07:29.763
[claps hands]

126
07:29.846 --> 07:32.683
If it comes to it, maybe we could hire temps as needed…

127
07:32.766 --> 07:34.601
Cooking is about teamwork.

128
07:34.685 --> 07:37.271
Only a team that's trained and practiced together

129
07:37.354 --> 07:39.189
will be able to serve the best food.

130
07:40.482 --> 07:42.985
No matter how hard any of us work,

131
07:43.068 --> 07:45.779
no one can handle a competition this big on their own.

132
07:49.116 --> 07:51.618
Well, that's just great… [sighs]

133
07:58.667 --> 07:59.793
Huh?

134
08:01.378 --> 08:02.879
Hello. Can I help you?

135
08:02.963 --> 08:05.340
Uh… Hello.

136
08:05.424 --> 08:09.886
I… I saw the kitchen staff job posting by the entrance.

137
08:16.768 --> 08:19.479
FAMIGLIA IS HIRING KITCHEN STAFF!

138
08:19.563 --> 08:21.189
PARK GEON-WOO AGE 29

139
08:31.366 --> 08:34.328
There's no need to be nervous. Go on, have some tea too.

140
08:34.411 --> 08:35.787
Oh, yes. Thank you so much.

141
08:40.792 --> 08:43.712
You studied culinary arts at a community college,

142
08:43.795 --> 08:45.464
and since you were 21,

143
08:45.547 --> 08:47.758
I see you got into restaurant work pretty young.

144
08:47.841 --> 08:49.885
And you're a traditional liquor sommelier.

145
08:49.968 --> 08:51.553
-[chuckles] -At age 23,

146
08:51.636 --> 08:53.805
you opened your own restaurant.

147
08:53.889 --> 08:55.724
Wow, that's quite impressive.

148
08:55.807 --> 08:57.851
-Italian, I see? -[chuckles]

149
08:57.934 --> 09:03.106
But why did it close after only about a year and a half?

150
09:03.190 --> 09:06.234
Ah, well, COVID suddenly hit, and things got hard.

151
09:06.777 --> 09:07.778
Oh, dear…

152
09:09.029 --> 09:10.989
What have you been doing for the past four years?

153
09:11.823 --> 09:13.158
Um…

154
09:13.241 --> 09:16.953
I closed down the restaurant and spent a year paying off my debts.

155
09:17.704 --> 09:19.331
And after that, I just…

156
09:20.374 --> 09:21.375
took some time off.

157
09:22.376 --> 09:24.252
So, no job?

158
09:24.336 --> 09:25.545
[chuckles] Right.

159
09:26.505 --> 09:28.924
Oh, I hadn't been cooking very long…

160
09:29.007 --> 09:30.050
[sucks teeth]

161
09:30.133 --> 09:32.803
…but for some reason, I was already feeling burned out.

162
09:32.886 --> 09:35.764
I wasn't even sure if I wanted to keep doing this.

163
09:35.847 --> 09:39.351
So I just spent… [chuckles] …all the money I had left traveling,

164
09:39.434 --> 09:43.105
reading and… Well, uh, that's… that's it.

165
09:43.688 --> 09:47.275
I thought maybe what I needed wasn't more technical training,

166
09:47.359 --> 09:51.905
but actually to learn more about people and the world.

167
09:52.572 --> 09:56.034
I felt that there might be insights that come from…

168
09:57.035 --> 09:58.703
from learning, not training.

169
10:00.080 --> 10:01.081
So…

170
10:02.791 --> 10:04.251
did you have an insight?

171
10:04.334 --> 10:06.169
Yes. [chuckles]

172
10:06.670 --> 10:10.090
[chuckles] Tell us. What was it?

173
10:10.799 --> 10:11.800
The insight

174
10:12.676 --> 10:13.718
was that

175
10:14.469 --> 10:15.720
there is no insight.

176
10:18.598 --> 10:22.144
I just wanted to get back into the kitchen. Like crazy.

177
10:25.439 --> 10:27.649
Here are the materials you asked for.

178
10:29.860 --> 10:33.321
It's our projected list of chefs likely to make the main round.

179
10:38.743 --> 10:40.495
The names without a check mark on the right

180
10:40.579 --> 10:43.206
haven't confirmed their participation yet.

181
10:45.834 --> 10:47.544
A few chefs based overseas

182
10:47.627 --> 10:51.590
also have yet to confirm either by phone or by email.

183
10:51.673 --> 10:54.551
I'll have our local branches meet them in person to get a firm answer.

184
10:55.552 --> 10:56.595
That's great.

185
10:57.512 --> 10:59.014
This will look strong.

186
10:59.097 --> 11:02.934
This looks like a good mix of domestic and overseas participants.

187
11:03.018 --> 11:05.228
We just need to land Joshua Yeong-ho Payton

188
11:05.312 --> 11:07.481
to make for a great first season.

189
11:07.564 --> 11:08.565
Yes.

190
11:08.648 --> 11:11.902
I will do whatever it takes to persuade Joshua Yeong-ho Payton.

191
11:11.985 --> 11:12.986
Hmm.

192
11:19.618 --> 11:20.702
Famiglia?

193
11:21.870 --> 11:24.039
Why is Famiglia on the list?

194
11:24.122 --> 11:25.707
Famiglia doesn't even have a chef,

195
11:25.790 --> 11:27.667
and you expect them to make the main round?

196
11:28.793 --> 11:29.836
Yes.

197
11:30.837 --> 11:31.963
[sighs]

198
11:35.800 --> 11:38.887
So tell me, why is Famiglia on this list all of a sudden?

199
11:39.471 --> 11:41.056
There are two reasons for that.

200
11:42.140 --> 11:47.771
First, they've agreed to enter and to drop their lawsuit against Pyeongyeon Group.

201
11:48.355 --> 11:50.524
-They're dropping the lawsuit? -Yes.

202
11:51.775 --> 11:55.654
The second reason is to get Chef Cha Woo-jin to enter the competition.

203
11:57.697 --> 12:02.327
Think of it as dropping one catfish into a tank full of minnows to stir them all up.

204
12:04.579 --> 12:06.289
[knife scraping]

205
12:22.764 --> 12:24.015
Yeong-su.

206
12:24.099 --> 12:25.100
Hmm?

207
12:26.101 --> 12:28.061
Isn't the sea bass for the main course?

208
12:28.144 --> 12:29.479
Yeah, it is.

209
12:29.563 --> 12:31.648
Then why did you bring it out? This isn't your station.

210
12:31.731 --> 12:32.732
Oh.

211
12:33.400 --> 12:35.902
The halibut for the ceviche wasn't in good shape,

212
12:35.986 --> 12:38.321
so I thought I'd try serving sea bass instead.

213
12:38.405 --> 12:40.991
I'm working on a sample for Chef Cha to try.

214
12:41.741 --> 12:43.577
-[sighs] -Ah.

215
12:43.660 --> 12:45.245
Oh, hey, man, my bad.

216
12:45.954 --> 12:47.872
I was in such a rush that I forgot to tell you.

217
12:47.956 --> 12:51.167
-[clicks tongues] Sorry, sorry. -[scoffs] Even if you were in a rush…

218
12:51.751 --> 12:53.420
[smacks lips] …we already portioned this out.

219
12:53.503 --> 12:56.298
You can't just use it however you want, huh? What are we supposed to do now?

220
12:56.965 --> 12:58.633
I said I get it. I'm sorry.

221
13:05.765 --> 13:07.142
[Yeong-su] Hey.

222
13:07.225 --> 13:08.226
Hey, Michael.

223
13:09.519 --> 13:12.606
[sighs] Geez, that melodramatic asshole. [clicks tongue]

224
13:13.440 --> 13:15.483
[scoffs, clicks tongue]

225
13:16.276 --> 13:18.194
Man, I'm so sick of this.

226
13:18.987 --> 13:20.780
[uneasy music playing]

227
13:26.870 --> 13:28.788
8 P.M. DINNER ALLERGENS AND NOTES

228
13:34.336 --> 13:36.630
[Woo-jin] Chairman Park has a shellfish allergy.

229
13:36.713 --> 13:38.340
Why isn't it here?

230
13:38.923 --> 13:40.842
The third course today is langoustine.

231
13:40.925 --> 13:42.135
LANGOUSTINE SMALL LOBSTERS

232
13:42.218 --> 13:43.511
I apologize, sir.

233
13:43.595 --> 13:45.055
I must've left it out by mistake.

234
13:45.639 --> 13:47.932
Once is a mistake. Twice is failure.

235
13:48.016 --> 13:49.934
Yes, Chef. It won't happen again.

236
13:56.524 --> 13:59.402
Can't you see that these chairs are off to one side?

237
13:59.486 --> 14:01.696
-Rearrange the chairs. -Yes, Chef.

238
14:03.198 --> 14:06.076
The flowers are wilting. Why didn't you replace them?

239
14:06.159 --> 14:07.160
[stammers]

240
14:07.243 --> 14:09.245
If you have time to think, move!

241
14:09.329 --> 14:11.039
-Get fresh flowers. -Yes, Chef.

242
14:24.552 --> 14:26.471
Drop the lighting two levels for dinner.

243
14:27.263 --> 14:28.640
I tell you this all the time.

244
14:28.723 --> 14:30.725
Dinner should be two levels dimmer than lunch.

245
14:31.393 --> 14:34.813
Who can have a glass of wine when it's this bright?

246
14:35.647 --> 14:39.025
Remember, fine dining is as much about getting people

247
14:39.109 --> 14:41.736
to drink more wine as it is about selling food.

248
14:41.820 --> 14:42.862
[all staff] Yes, Chef!

249
14:43.863 --> 14:45.198
[Jeong-won] Right.

250
14:45.281 --> 14:46.783
As you can see from the report,

251
14:46.866 --> 14:49.911
Infinite Dining is currently trending at number one.

252
14:49.994 --> 14:51.496
-I see. -[knocking on door]

253
14:51.579 --> 14:52.956
[door opens]

254
14:57.752 --> 14:58.920
Wow.

255
14:59.963 --> 15:01.673
I didn't know you had company.

256
15:03.341 --> 15:05.343
[inhales sharply] What was so urgent

257
15:05.427 --> 15:09.013
that you had to come all the way to the chairwoman's office yourself, Ms. Seon?

258
15:10.056 --> 15:13.518
If you'd reported it to me, I would have brought it to her myself.

259
15:14.185 --> 15:15.311
I called her in.

260
15:18.064 --> 15:21.651
All right, I'll get going then. I have a meeting in ten minutes.

261
15:21.735 --> 15:22.736
[Hae-seon] Okay.

262
15:35.290 --> 15:36.833
[door closes]

263
15:37.542 --> 15:39.961
Let me see, judging by the look on your face,

264
15:40.044 --> 15:42.756
Ms. Seon must be doing a good job.

265
15:44.340 --> 15:47.093
Even if you had important business with her,

266
15:47.177 --> 15:49.471
last I heard, Seon Jeong-won works for me.

267
15:50.597 --> 15:55.727
So now, would it kill her to give me even a quick briefing before coming to see you?

268
15:55.810 --> 15:57.562
[scoffs]

269
15:58.396 --> 16:00.190
[clicks tongue] Then again,

270
16:00.273 --> 16:02.650
Jeong-won's always been thorough and good at her job.

271
16:04.027 --> 16:08.448
Ah! Young people really know how to get things done properly.

272
16:08.531 --> 16:10.658
[clicks tongue] Old folks like me

273
16:10.742 --> 16:13.536
should just watch from the sidelines and clap, I suppose.

274
16:13.620 --> 16:15.538
Whoo!

275
16:18.583 --> 16:19.918
That's bitter.

276
16:20.001 --> 16:22.962
[clicks tongue] Bitter on the tongue, bitter in life…

277
16:24.547 --> 16:25.924
Do you mind if I have a candy?

278
16:31.471 --> 16:33.848
[smacks lips] That's so sweet. Mmm.

279
16:33.932 --> 16:36.351
Famiglia says they'll drop the lawsuit.

280
16:36.434 --> 16:37.811
[coughs]

281
16:40.104 --> 16:42.065
And apparently, they're entering the competition too.

282
16:42.148 --> 16:45.193
-[coughing] -[candy clatters on table]

283
16:45.276 --> 16:46.528
Wait, Famiglia?

284
16:46.611 --> 16:49.280
How are they entering the competition without a chef?

285
16:50.949 --> 16:53.660
These are the most probable to make the main round.

286
17:01.125 --> 17:02.252
Ha!

287
17:02.961 --> 17:05.421
[cackling]

288
17:05.505 --> 17:07.340
This is absurd.

289
17:08.800 --> 17:11.219
Wow. That Seon Jeong-won…

290
17:11.302 --> 17:13.805
[laughs] Is she really that idealistic,

291
17:13.888 --> 17:16.474
or is she deliberately trying to create drama?

292
17:16.558 --> 17:19.894
[laughing] This is too funny. Seriously.

293
17:19.978 --> 17:23.147
It's good they're dropping the lawsuit before the competition…

294
17:27.277 --> 17:29.863
but we can't have Famiglia attracting any attention.

295
17:35.952 --> 17:38.288
Creating some drama is all right,

296
17:38.371 --> 17:42.584
but the star of that show should be actually someone that the producers cast.

297
17:43.126 --> 17:45.336
Not some outsider who just wandered in.

298
17:49.549 --> 17:50.967
Am I right, Ms. Baek?

299
17:52.218 --> 17:53.553
Famiglia.

300
17:54.137 --> 17:56.764
Famiglia is actually entering the competition.

301
17:56.848 --> 17:59.392
[inhales sharply] Someone suddenly shows up

302
17:59.475 --> 18:04.230
and leads Famiglia, a restaurant on its last legs, into the competition.

303
18:05.356 --> 18:06.399
But who? Why?

304
18:06.482 --> 18:09.986
Besides, they're projected to make the main round?

305
18:11.195 --> 18:14.908
Famiglia is projected to make the main round?

306
18:16.534 --> 18:18.161
[inhales]

307
18:18.244 --> 18:21.748
Seeing as Seon Jeong-won is sharp as a tack…

308
18:24.667 --> 18:25.668
[beeps]

309
18:26.252 --> 18:27.712
Tell Jeon to come in right now.

310
18:28.421 --> 18:29.923
PARTICIPANTS LIKELY TO REACH MAIN ROUND

311
18:31.174 --> 18:32.926
[knocking on door]

312
18:33.009 --> 18:34.260
Come in.

313
18:40.099 --> 18:41.225
You called for me, ma'am?

314
18:42.393 --> 18:43.394
Sit down.

315
18:47.231 --> 18:49.359
There's something I need you to look into.

316
18:50.068 --> 18:51.110
Okay.

317
18:52.278 --> 18:54.697
-Famiglia. -Famiglia. Famiglia?

318
18:56.616 --> 18:59.911
Wait, you mean the late Chef Choi Seung-hyo's Famiglia?

319
18:59.994 --> 19:00.995
That's right.

320
19:01.496 --> 19:04.123
-That damn Famiglia. -[exhales deeply]

321
19:04.666 --> 19:07.168
Some rando showed up in their kitchen out of nowhere

322
19:07.251 --> 19:11.130
like some gunslinger riding in from the wilderness. [inhales sharply]

323
19:11.214 --> 19:15.218
Anyway, he's definitely got serious skills. [sucks teeth]

324
19:15.301 --> 19:19.138
Considering he's leading Famiglia into this competition as a head chef.

325
19:20.139 --> 19:22.100
Ah, come on, boss.

326
19:22.767 --> 19:24.769
How on earth is that possible, huh?

327
19:24.852 --> 19:28.606
[sucks teeth] The chef de partie handling ingredients definitely quit back then.

328
19:28.690 --> 19:31.734
So then there shouldn't be anyone left. Except that useless woman!

329
19:36.322 --> 19:38.157
Look into it quietly.

330
19:38.241 --> 19:40.535
I want you to find out who this new chef is,

331
19:40.618 --> 19:43.538
where he's been and what he's been doing over there.

332
19:43.621 --> 19:45.373
How he's connected to Famiglia,

333
19:45.456 --> 19:48.501
and why he wants to enter this competition in the first place!

334
19:48.584 --> 19:50.837
Yes. Okay. Understood.

335
19:50.920 --> 19:54.424
But do not rush it too much. Do it right!

336
19:55.758 --> 19:56.843
Hey, Jeon.

337
19:56.926 --> 19:58.219
Yes? Uh…

338
19:58.302 --> 20:02.098
If you end up botching this operation, like you did with Choi Seung-hyo…

339
20:04.142 --> 20:05.518
it will be your last task.

340
20:06.310 --> 20:07.645
Understood. Yes, ma'am.

341
20:17.989 --> 20:19.365
[Han] Vegetable stew.

342
20:19.449 --> 20:21.034
It seems simple enough,

343
20:21.117 --> 20:24.245
but it's an excellent dish for testing basic skills.

344
20:52.440 --> 20:54.817
The ability to manage workspace and hygiene.

345
20:54.901 --> 20:56.277
[sizzling]

346
21:05.119 --> 21:06.204
[tapping utensil on bowl]

347
21:27.183 --> 21:29.435
[Han] One person sautés the vegetables over high heat

348
21:29.519 --> 21:31.437
and reduces the stock over low heat.

349
21:33.648 --> 21:35.149
The other does the reverse,

350
21:35.233 --> 21:37.401
sautéing the vegetables slowly over low heat

351
21:37.485 --> 21:39.320
before reducing the stock over high heat.

352
21:41.322 --> 21:42.698
There is no right answer.

353
21:42.782 --> 21:45.326
Cooking is ever-evolving.

354
21:48.287 --> 21:50.414
[Song-yi] Auntie Du-yeong is going to be sous-chef?

355
21:53.501 --> 21:57.171
Well, see, Geon-woo's stew was actually better tasting.

356
21:57.839 --> 22:01.092
But the most important skills for a sous-chef

357
22:01.175 --> 22:03.719
are workspace management and hygiene.

358
22:04.303 --> 22:06.139
Everything has to stay organized,

359
22:06.222 --> 22:09.892
and the ingredients need to be sorted, so you know what's what at a glance.

360
22:09.976 --> 22:12.436
Especially in a competition like this where every second matters,

361
22:12.520 --> 22:15.439
those skills are absolutely essential for the sous-chef.

362
22:16.899 --> 22:20.027
When it comes to prepping ingredients and handling heat better,

363
22:20.736 --> 22:23.364
the more experienced Chef Geon-woo has the edge.

364
22:23.447 --> 22:29.579
But he's weaker at organizing and at sorting the ingredients for easy access.

365
22:29.662 --> 22:30.788
[smacks lips]

366
22:30.872 --> 22:32.582
That's an innate trait.

367
22:33.416 --> 22:36.502
Chef Choi Du-yeong has a natural instinct.

368
22:36.586 --> 22:38.838
People like her are born for this kind of thing.

369
22:42.258 --> 22:45.553
So Chef Choi Du-yeong will be sous-chef,

370
22:45.636 --> 22:47.847
and Chef Park Geon-Woo will handle garde-manger.

371
22:47.930 --> 22:49.599
GARDE-MANGER - RESPONSIBLE FOR BASIC PREPARATION

372
22:49.682 --> 22:52.059
-Understood. -Okay. Head chef,

373
22:52.143 --> 22:54.061
sous-chef, garde-manger…

374
22:55.479 --> 22:59.066
Now we just need a junior to handle odd jobs and dishwashing…

375
22:59.650 --> 23:00.902
[inhales deeply]

376
23:03.654 --> 23:05.656
[whimsical music playing]

377
23:17.001 --> 23:18.085
Huh?

378
23:19.003 --> 23:20.004
[Song-yi] No way.

379
23:20.546 --> 23:21.714
I mean, I can't do it.

380
23:21.797 --> 23:23.424
Uh, why can't you do it?

381
23:23.507 --> 23:24.508
Because…

382
23:25.259 --> 23:28.471
[sighs] Well, because I just can't. I can't do it.

383
23:28.554 --> 23:30.765
I've never cooked before, and I'm useless at it.

384
23:30.848 --> 23:31.849
Besides,

385
23:32.433 --> 23:33.976
I don't want to do it.

386
23:34.060 --> 23:35.311
I've always been scared of knives.

387
23:35.394 --> 23:38.314
Do things that don't require a knife. Like washing dishes.

388
23:38.397 --> 23:40.566
I still just can't do it.

389
23:41.150 --> 23:42.652
I have an allergy.

390
23:42.735 --> 23:45.154
An allergy? Allergy to what?

391
23:48.282 --> 23:49.408
Tap water.

392
23:49.492 --> 23:52.078
I'm allergic to tap water so I can't wash dishes either.

393
23:52.161 --> 23:53.537
What?

394
23:53.621 --> 23:55.665
[sighs] Anyway, I'm not doing it.

395
23:55.748 --> 23:57.917
I'm not going into the kitchen. [huffs]

396
23:58.417 --> 23:59.418
Hey, Song.

397
24:00.878 --> 24:01.879
[sighs]

398
24:02.380 --> 24:04.131
Allergic to tap water?

399
24:10.763 --> 24:12.139
[sighs]

400
24:12.223 --> 24:14.475
That was close. I almost ended up in the kitchen.

401
24:15.851 --> 24:17.853
[sighs] That would've been a disaster.

402
24:17.937 --> 24:20.856
When seasoning meat, do so evenly on both sides.

403
24:20.940 --> 24:23.150
A beefsteak should only be flipped once.

404
24:23.943 --> 24:27.113
Always use black pepper for its stronger aroma and flavor.

405
24:27.196 --> 24:30.366
For light-colored dishes that could look messy, use white pepper.

406
24:30.449 --> 24:32.118
What on earth are you talking about?

407
24:32.201 --> 24:33.953
Always sharpen knives on a whetstone.

408
24:34.036 --> 24:36.580
Once at 1,000 grit, then again at 8,000.

409
24:36.664 --> 24:38.624
-Excuse me? -Cook dried pasta

410
24:38.708 --> 24:41.460
two or three minutes less than the package says.

411
24:41.544 --> 24:43.713
It'll finish cooking in the saucepan.

412
24:43.796 --> 24:45.548
And always save the pasta water.

413
24:46.132 --> 24:47.383
Listen, Chef Kran…

414
24:47.967 --> 24:48.968
Krantzwerst!

415
24:49.051 --> 24:52.263
Just memorize that much for now. You can learn the rest as we go.

416
24:52.930 --> 24:54.890
The junior's jobs are much simpler anyway.

417
24:56.767 --> 25:00.062
[inhales sharply] Also, just call me Chris. Chris.

418
25:00.855 --> 25:02.940
I am not cooking, Chris.

419
25:03.024 --> 25:05.026
I own the restaurant and run the floor.

420
25:05.109 --> 25:06.402
I'm not a chef, okay?

421
25:07.194 --> 25:08.195
-Okay. -[sighs]

422
25:08.904 --> 25:09.905
So what?

423
25:10.489 --> 25:12.366
You can start learning now.

424
25:12.950 --> 25:14.535
You own a restaurant.

425
25:14.618 --> 25:16.620
You should at least know the basics of cooking.

426
25:16.704 --> 25:18.539
-And if I say no? -Then find one.

427
25:18.622 --> 25:20.416
-Find what? -A chef.

428
25:22.668 --> 25:25.588
I thought we needed a four-member team. We're not competing?

429
25:26.881 --> 25:28.966
Even if we start practicing around the clock right now,

430
25:29.050 --> 25:30.426
there's no guarantee we'll go far.

431
25:30.509 --> 25:33.179
How much longer are you willing to wait for someone to show up?

432
25:34.221 --> 25:35.222
[sighs]

433
25:36.640 --> 25:38.559
[sighs] Hey.

434
25:39.518 --> 25:41.937
Do you think I want a beginner? Of course, I don't.

435
25:43.064 --> 25:45.566
But for now, this is the only option that we have.

436
25:50.946 --> 25:51.947
Hmm?

437
25:53.908 --> 25:54.909
Okay, fine.

438
25:55.576 --> 25:58.871
But look, only until we find someone to replace me.

439
25:59.580 --> 26:02.416
The day we hire new kitchen staff, I'm done working in the kitchen.

440
26:03.209 --> 26:04.210
[huffs]

441
26:06.379 --> 26:07.880
Okay.

442
26:07.963 --> 26:09.256
Deal.

443
26:23.437 --> 26:25.856
[Han] Who sprinkles salt from that high up?

444
26:27.191 --> 26:28.943
Where did you pick up that flashy move?

445
26:29.026 --> 26:32.279
Sprinkle the salt from closer up. That way, it seasons evenly.

446
26:35.324 --> 26:37.952
I told you not to let the flame extend past the pan!

447
26:38.786 --> 26:41.664
How many times do I have to tell you? It'll burn the sides.

448
26:43.082 --> 26:44.875
Match the flame to the size of the pan.

449
26:49.588 --> 26:50.756
Repeat.

450
26:50.840 --> 26:53.175
"Match the flame to the size of the pan."

451
26:54.051 --> 26:56.595
-Match the flame to the size of the-- -Louder!

452
26:57.763 --> 27:00.516
[louder] Match the flame to the size of the pan.

453
27:02.768 --> 27:05.396
Again? I told you, meat goes in at the smoking point.

454
27:05.479 --> 27:08.190
Coat the pan with oil, and when it's smoking like crazy,

455
27:08.274 --> 27:10.317
count to 20, then put the meat in.

456
27:10.401 --> 27:12.653
[imitates sizzling] Like this.

457
27:12.736 --> 27:15.531
[imitates sizzling] You want a loud sizzle like that.

458
27:15.614 --> 27:16.907
No sound, no color.

459
27:16.991 --> 27:18.993
No color, no taste. Okay?

460
27:21.495 --> 27:22.496
[sighs]

461
27:29.170 --> 27:30.171
[gasps softly]

462
27:30.754 --> 27:32.006
Um, by the way,

463
27:33.215 --> 27:34.925
could you stop speaking so fast?

464
27:35.009 --> 27:37.761
I already have too much to learn. It's confusing.

465
27:39.054 --> 27:40.139
Hmm?

466
27:40.222 --> 27:42.099
Chris, you need to speak more clearly.

467
27:42.183 --> 27:44.685
I can barely understand you most of the time.

468
27:44.768 --> 27:46.520
Stop trying to be flashy.

469
27:46.604 --> 27:48.647
And say it in a normal way. A normal way.

470
27:51.275 --> 27:52.443
Hmm.

471
27:54.403 --> 27:56.614
Back straight, chin up.

472
28:02.953 --> 28:05.080
[breathes shakily] I'm going crazy.

473
28:05.164 --> 28:07.541
What if someone ends up getting hurt or something?

474
28:07.625 --> 28:10.211
I told you to be careful when you're holding a knife!

475
28:12.004 --> 28:14.632
What did I tell you earlier? Three-finger rule.

476
28:15.299 --> 28:17.551
Like this. Curl your fingers at the first joint.

477
28:19.637 --> 28:21.555
Curl them in further. Like this.

478
28:22.473 --> 28:23.474
Hold it.

479
28:24.225 --> 28:25.226
Now look.

480
28:26.185 --> 28:28.145
Grip the knife farther forward.

481
28:29.730 --> 28:30.856
Closer to the blade.

482
28:32.566 --> 28:33.984
[exhales sharply]

483
28:34.485 --> 28:38.781
When slicing, push the blade gently forward.

484
28:40.783 --> 28:43.118
Put some weight behind the knife, like this.

485
29:03.764 --> 29:04.807
Good.

486
29:19.530 --> 29:21.031
[screams]

487
29:23.033 --> 29:26.579
[chuckles] Why are you so startled? It's just a little cut.

488
29:27.663 --> 29:28.664
See what I mean?

489
29:28.747 --> 29:30.040
See what?

490
29:30.124 --> 29:31.792
I told you I shouldn't be in the kitchen.

491
29:31.875 --> 29:34.295
Now I cut your finger off. That's why I don't cook.

492
29:34.378 --> 29:35.546
[breathes shakily]

493
29:36.130 --> 29:38.507
-[sighs] -[running footsteps]

494
29:53.272 --> 29:54.273
Oh, boy.

495
29:55.149 --> 29:57.735
Try to understand. She has her reasons.

496
29:57.818 --> 29:58.944
What?

497
29:59.028 --> 30:02.239
Go easy on her. Ms. Choi never set foot in the kitchen.

498
30:03.240 --> 30:05.784
[chuckling] Why not? Does she never cook for herself?

499
30:06.493 --> 30:10.039
She eats what we make or goes out to eat somewhere.

500
30:11.582 --> 30:13.167
[sighs] Well, you see…

501
30:15.294 --> 30:16.795
[eerie music playing]

502
30:16.879 --> 30:17.963
It's the ghost.

503
30:18.964 --> 30:19.965
A ghost?

504
30:20.049 --> 30:22.593
Here's the thing… [inhales sharply]

505
30:23.636 --> 30:25.095
There's a ghost…

506
30:26.680 --> 30:28.015
on her shoulder.

507
30:29.391 --> 30:30.768
[laughing]

508
30:30.851 --> 30:32.269
Well, it's one of those things.

509
30:32.353 --> 30:35.564
Chris, you're too American, so you wouldn't get it even if I explained.

510
30:38.692 --> 30:39.693
[Du-yeong giggles]

511
30:40.694 --> 30:41.987
[chuckles]

512
30:51.163 --> 30:53.123
My dad used to sleep in this room.

513
30:53.207 --> 30:55.542
I cleared out most of his clothes and things,

514
30:56.835 --> 30:58.462
but I left the furniture.

515
31:00.172 --> 31:01.173
[Han sighs]

516
31:04.551 --> 31:06.303
[gentle music playing]

517
31:22.486 --> 31:25.072
-Is something wrong? -Hmm?

518
31:25.906 --> 31:28.867
Oh… No, it's nothing.

519
31:30.160 --> 31:32.538
The bathroom's to the right. My room's across the hall.

520
31:32.621 --> 31:35.833
So please don't hesitate to knock if you need anything.

521
31:42.423 --> 31:43.674
-[grunts] -If you want coffee,

522
31:43.757 --> 31:46.677
there's a machine next to the sink. The instructions are on the wall.

523
31:46.760 --> 31:49.596
So I don't think you should have any trouble using it.

524
31:50.556 --> 31:51.890
I got it.

525
31:53.767 --> 31:54.768
[scoffs]

526
31:57.521 --> 31:58.689
What is that thing?

527
32:01.150 --> 32:02.443
This is my friend.

528
32:04.611 --> 32:05.612
[chuckles]

529
32:12.327 --> 32:15.664
But are you sure you don't have to go back to the States?

530
32:16.373 --> 32:18.917
You'd be breaching your contract. Is that really okay?

531
32:20.377 --> 32:23.797
I'll go back in three months. I'll just have to pay a fine.

532
32:23.881 --> 32:25.632
The prize money is 500 million.

533
32:25.716 --> 32:27.342
I'll just pay it off with some of that.

534
32:28.218 --> 32:29.219
What?

535
32:29.303 --> 32:30.721
[Du-yeong] Song-yi!

536
32:30.804 --> 32:33.056
Song-yi! The front door's broken again!

537
32:33.140 --> 32:34.892
-Come down here! -Coming, Auntie.

538
32:34.975 --> 32:37.644
Oh, I left my phone downstairs. [chuckles]

539
32:37.728 --> 32:39.271
Coming right down, Auntie!

540
32:45.819 --> 32:47.321
This is the right move, right?

541
32:53.327 --> 32:55.329
I should do this, right?

542
32:55.412 --> 32:56.830
[whirring]

543
32:56.914 --> 32:59.249
Hello! Have a wonderful day.

544
32:59.333 --> 33:00.793
[chuckles]

545
33:02.920 --> 33:05.130
-[chuckles] I hope. -[trilling]

546
33:13.806 --> 33:14.807
[Henri] Mmm.

547
33:17.392 --> 33:20.187
Is this what you call "maesil-jangajji"?

548
33:20.854 --> 33:25.442
It's interesting. It tastes like umeboshi, but a great pairing with Western food.

549
33:26.860 --> 33:29.905
Well, should we call this Korean cuisine?

550
33:29.988 --> 33:31.323
Japanese cuisine?

551
33:31.406 --> 33:33.116
Or maybe…

552
33:33.200 --> 33:34.284
French?

553
33:35.452 --> 33:37.788
Um… [chuckles]

554
33:37.871 --> 33:40.082
Actually, I guess, none of them.

555
33:40.749 --> 33:43.836
It's simply a dish made by a Korean chef.

556
33:44.711 --> 33:47.381
I believe the days of drawing national boundaries

557
33:47.464 --> 33:49.424
around cuisine are finally over.

558
33:50.092 --> 33:52.511
Now we need to look at it more closely.

559
33:53.595 --> 33:57.599
We're trying to find something universal within what is distinctly Korean.

560
33:57.683 --> 34:00.269
Through that process, we can discover the identity

561
34:00.352 --> 34:03.647
and future of what we now call Korean cuisine.

562
34:04.606 --> 34:07.818
What matters isn't finding the best Korean dish.

563
34:07.901 --> 34:09.361
It's finding the best Korean chef.

564
34:09.945 --> 34:12.114
We're interested in people, after all.

565
34:13.073 --> 34:17.369
We may not be able to define exactly what K-food is through a single competition,

566
34:17.452 --> 34:19.621
but if we keep the focus on the people,

567
34:19.705 --> 34:21.039
we'll gradually develop

568
34:21.123 --> 34:24.334
a clear standard for what K-food is and what it should be

569
34:24.418 --> 34:26.295
as the competition continues.

570
34:33.093 --> 34:35.721
[sighs] Would you like anything else?

571
34:35.804 --> 34:37.264
How's the food?

572
34:37.347 --> 34:38.849
Like the name of the restaurant.

573
34:39.725 --> 34:41.184
Exception.

574
34:46.398 --> 34:48.233
-Mmm. -[Woo-jin inhales deeply]

575
34:51.486 --> 34:54.573
By the way, I keep thinking about Chef Choi Seung-hyo.

576
34:56.033 --> 34:57.576
An absolute tragedy.

577
34:58.952 --> 35:01.496
I guess Famiglia will be closing down soon.

578
35:02.664 --> 35:05.083
I really am terribly sorry.

579
35:07.753 --> 35:09.630
It might not actually close.

580
35:13.050 --> 35:14.217
It's not closing?

581
35:15.260 --> 35:18.055
A new head chef is taking over Famiglia.

582
35:18.138 --> 35:19.640
Actually, he's starting today.

583
35:20.766 --> 35:22.601
[Henri] Really? Is that true?

584
35:22.684 --> 35:24.478
Who is he, this new chef?

585
35:24.561 --> 35:28.607
He's a rising star in the US and Europe right now.

586
35:28.690 --> 35:31.735
He's a Korean chef named Chris K.

587
35:31.818 --> 35:34.613
He's based in New York, but he's in Korea now.

588
35:34.696 --> 35:36.698
That very Chris K.…

589
35:39.368 --> 35:41.078
has agreed to lead Famiglia

590
35:41.787 --> 35:45.290
in The Table: K-Chef 2026 so they could compete.

591
35:50.003 --> 35:52.673
[host] The winner of the Grand Prix is…

592
35:52.756 --> 35:54.091
Congratulations!

593
35:54.174 --> 35:56.426
-Aurelia from the USA! -[cheering]

594
35:59.596 --> 36:02.432
-[cheering continues] -Yeah!

595
36:04.017 --> 36:05.852
[cheering, applause continue]

596
36:12.693 --> 36:14.027
[chef] That's him.

597
36:14.111 --> 36:16.321
-[chef 2] Who? -[chef 1] Chris K.

598
36:16.405 --> 36:17.406
[chef 2] Chris K.?

599
36:17.489 --> 36:19.491
[chef 1] Korean sous-chef from the American team?

600
36:19.574 --> 36:21.076
The team that won the Grand Prix?

601
36:21.159 --> 36:22.160
Oh, really?

602
36:23.495 --> 36:26.623
But then why is everyone crowded around the sous-chef?

603
36:26.707 --> 36:28.458
Wait. You haven't heard?

604
36:29.001 --> 36:30.544
They say he's practically the head chef.

605
36:30.627 --> 36:33.046
[chef 2] What? The sous-chef is the head chef?

606
36:33.130 --> 36:34.214
[chef 1] Yeah.

607
36:34.297 --> 36:38.051
People say the winning concept was totally his idea.

608
36:38.135 --> 36:39.344
[chef 2] Seriously?

609
36:39.428 --> 36:41.179
So, you're telling me that that dish

610
36:41.263 --> 36:45.058
that came out that looked like magic came from that Korean guy?

611
36:45.142 --> 36:46.518
[chef 1] I'm still shocked.

612
36:46.601 --> 36:49.229
I don't even know how he came up with a dish like that.

613
36:49.312 --> 36:50.313
[chef 2] Yeah.

614
36:50.397 --> 36:53.608
The score gap was huge between the first and second awards.

615
36:54.693 --> 36:56.153
Undisputed victory.

616
36:58.155 --> 36:59.406
[sighs]

617
37:11.001 --> 37:12.252
Peel it thin.

618
37:12.335 --> 37:13.336
Oh, yes.

619
37:20.135 --> 37:21.636
No. Turn it off.

620
37:24.222 --> 37:25.390
What did I tell you?

621
37:25.474 --> 37:26.641
When you baste with butter,

622
37:26.725 --> 37:29.186
do it quickly 30 to 35 times.

623
37:29.269 --> 37:31.396
Then flip it and baste another 20 times.

624
37:32.147 --> 37:33.899
Chef Geon-woo, you too.

625
37:33.982 --> 37:34.983
Oh, yes, Chef.

626
37:37.277 --> 37:39.529
The reason we arroser with clarified butter

627
37:39.613 --> 37:41.448
is in order to speed up the Maillard reaction.

628
37:41.531 --> 37:43.325
Keep the intervals consistent.

629
37:43.950 --> 37:46.661
As fast as you can, but keep it real steady.

630
37:46.745 --> 37:49.456
That's why we never put more than two pieces in a pan.

631
37:49.539 --> 37:51.958
It's hard to arroser three at once.

632
37:53.126 --> 37:56.505
Learn to feel the right temperature without using a thermometer.

633
37:56.588 --> 37:57.923
Study. Practice.

634
37:59.132 --> 38:00.342
Got it?

635
38:00.425 --> 38:02.677
If you can't even do this, forget winning.

636
38:02.761 --> 38:04.888
We won't even get to the finals. Okay?

637
38:05.597 --> 38:06.598
-Okay. -Okay.

638
38:07.516 --> 38:09.392
What? Winning?

639
38:10.977 --> 38:12.729
Yes. Winning.

640
38:18.568 --> 38:21.196
Why, what's the matter? Don't you want Famiglia to win?

641
38:21.279 --> 38:22.489
Why enter at all then?

642
38:22.572 --> 38:23.782
Do you have time to waste?

643
38:23.865 --> 38:26.201
-Well… -[Geon-woo] No, but… [sighs]

644
38:26.785 --> 38:28.161
Hurry up and do it again.

645
38:28.245 --> 38:30.205
Miss the serving window, and the food suffers.

646
38:30.288 --> 38:33.875
And remember, customers don't taste with just their mouths.

647
38:34.459 --> 38:35.669
They feel it with their hearts.

648
38:36.670 --> 38:40.257
-If the food is late, you lose them. -[sighs]

649
38:40.340 --> 38:41.466
-Okay. Get a move on. -[claps hands]

650
38:41.550 --> 38:42.592
Let's do it again. Let's go.

651
38:42.676 --> 38:44.010
-Yes, Chef! -[Du-yeong] Yes, Chef!

652
38:58.441 --> 38:59.442
Mr. Park?

653
39:00.527 --> 39:03.780
Why are the sauce and stock containers all over the place?

654
39:03.864 --> 39:05.365
Put them back where they belong, please.

655
39:05.448 --> 39:08.827
Oh, okay. I was going to do that after I finished rinsing this.

656
39:08.910 --> 39:10.871
What are you talking about? There's an order to things.

657
39:10.954 --> 39:14.040
Put all of those away first, then you get to do the washing.

658
39:15.542 --> 39:16.751
[Geon-woo grunts]

659
39:16.835 --> 39:18.753
Yes, understood, Chef.

660
39:20.213 --> 39:22.382
You didn't even dry your hands. [gasps]

661
39:22.465 --> 39:24.092
There's water dripping all over the floor.

662
39:24.176 --> 39:27.137
What if someone steps in it, slips and gets hurt? Then what?

663
39:27.220 --> 39:30.265
[chuckles] No one's gonna slip on a few drops.

664
39:30.348 --> 39:31.808
"A few drops"?

665
39:31.892 --> 39:33.935
Didn't you hear what Chef Chris said?

666
39:34.019 --> 39:35.061
There's rules.

667
39:36.646 --> 39:37.689
Yes, Chef.

668
39:38.440 --> 39:39.566
[sighs]

669
39:40.233 --> 39:41.234
What's this?

670
39:42.402 --> 39:44.946
You can't rinse the pans and leave them like that. Huh?

671
39:45.030 --> 39:46.823
You have to dry them with a dry cloth and put them away.

672
39:46.907 --> 39:47.908
I was about to do it,

673
39:47.991 --> 39:50.410
but you told me to put away the sauce containers first.

674
39:50.493 --> 39:52.829
Don't you know that cast iron pans rust if you don't dry them?

675
39:52.913 --> 39:54.372
-[sighs] -You're supposed to know that.

676
39:54.456 --> 39:56.583
-That's basic knowledge. -Excuse me.

677
39:58.877 --> 40:02.714
[scoffs] Tell me. How long have you been cooking?

678
40:03.715 --> 40:05.300
A year? Two?

679
40:05.926 --> 40:09.012
[chuckles] I've been working in kitchens for over eight years.

680
40:09.596 --> 40:12.974
I know enough to know what I'm doing, you know?

681
40:13.058 --> 40:15.310
I don't know why… [chuckles]

682
40:15.393 --> 40:17.437
…the head chef made you sous-chef,

683
40:17.520 --> 40:20.106
but I respect his decision, so quit the drama, okay?

684
40:21.274 --> 40:23.235
I have my own way and my rules.

685
40:23.318 --> 40:27.405
I'd really appreciate it if… [chuckles] …you please respected that.

686
40:28.531 --> 40:30.450
And let me say another thing.

687
40:31.034 --> 40:33.036
When you rest meat, flip it once halfway through.

688
40:33.119 --> 40:35.538
Don't just leave it sitting on one side.

689
40:35.622 --> 40:39.376
That way, the juices redistribute evenly.

690
40:39.459 --> 40:42.337
You should at least know that much. You're the sous-chef.

691
40:43.964 --> 40:45.257
[sighs]

692
40:51.221 --> 40:52.264
[sighs]

693
40:57.394 --> 40:58.770
[tires screech]

694
41:31.011 --> 41:32.012
Who are you?

695
41:33.346 --> 41:34.347
[scoffs]

696
41:34.431 --> 41:36.016
What brings you here?

697
41:50.363 --> 41:51.364
So it is you.

698
41:59.664 --> 42:01.082
Chris K.

699
42:04.210 --> 42:05.337
[chuckles]

700
42:08.965 --> 42:11.301
You're treated like royalty in the US.

701
42:12.010 --> 42:14.304
So, why are you hanging around a dump like this?

702
42:15.638 --> 42:16.639
Care to explain?

703
42:16.723 --> 42:19.100
Why on earth should I explain myself to you?

704
42:23.229 --> 42:24.898
You were rude to me first.

705
42:26.316 --> 42:27.525
[sighs]

706
42:27.609 --> 42:29.110
If that's all…

707
42:33.615 --> 42:35.075
Why are you here?

708
42:36.326 --> 42:38.286
What's your connection to Famiglia?

709
42:39.496 --> 42:40.997
I hear you're competing.

710
42:49.547 --> 42:50.548
Then again…

711
42:52.467 --> 42:54.469
I suppose none of that matters.

712
42:57.263 --> 42:58.306
What matters is…

713
43:00.683 --> 43:02.185
who is going to win

714
43:02.811 --> 43:04.437
in the end.

715
43:06.356 --> 43:08.942
Pyeongyeon threw this competition together in a hurry.

716
43:09.025 --> 43:11.194
I figured it'd just be a bunch of hacks turning up.

717
43:12.320 --> 43:13.571
Glad I was wrong.

718
43:14.697 --> 43:15.824
This might be fun.

719
43:16.741 --> 43:18.701
Right. See you soon, buddy.

720
43:21.329 --> 43:22.330
Hey.

721
43:24.499 --> 43:26.167
Don't worry.

722
43:29.629 --> 43:31.214
Because in the end,

723
43:32.048 --> 43:34.467
you'll lose to me again anyway.

724
43:34.551 --> 43:36.177
Just like seven years ago.

725
43:39.389 --> 43:40.390
And…

726
43:42.225 --> 43:43.560
you'll regret it.

727
43:47.272 --> 43:49.399
[Han] You'll regret what you did that day.

728
44:04.456 --> 44:06.458
[sighs deeply]

729
44:08.418 --> 44:10.378
[whines] No.

730
44:18.595 --> 44:19.596
Hmm.

731
44:25.143 --> 44:27.145
Song-yi. Where are you going?

732
44:27.228 --> 44:30.899
Oh. Just out front. Real quick.

733
44:31.566 --> 44:32.859
[Han] Where are you going?

734
44:34.194 --> 44:35.528
We need to start practicing now.

735
44:35.612 --> 44:38.865
[gasps] Oh, sorry. It's really urgent.

736
44:38.948 --> 44:40.658
We can practice tomorrow.

737
44:43.661 --> 44:46.039
[sighs] We don't have that much time left.

738
44:47.373 --> 44:51.127
Let's start tomorrow. I'll work really hard. I promise.

739
44:52.378 --> 44:56.090
Please. Just, uh… Just for today. Today.

740
45:00.220 --> 45:01.971
[clicks tongue] Okay.

741
45:02.055 --> 45:03.056
Okay.

742
45:08.436 --> 45:09.771
[Du-yeong sighs]

743
45:11.439 --> 45:13.608
[clicks tongue] I am really worried though.

744
45:15.193 --> 45:17.237
That Song-yi has to work in the kitchen.

745
45:21.324 --> 45:24.869
[Du-yeong] It's something of an open secret at Famiglia.

746
45:24.953 --> 45:27.205
That she's haunted by a ghost.

747
45:27.288 --> 45:28.289
[Han] A ghost?

748
45:28.998 --> 45:31.042
Really, a ghost?

749
45:31.125 --> 45:32.418
Let me see if I understand you.

750
45:33.253 --> 45:34.671
Ms. Choi has a ghost on her?

751
45:34.754 --> 45:35.880
[Du-yeong] Mm-hmm.

752
45:35.964 --> 45:38.216
At the beginning, everyone thought,

753
45:38.299 --> 45:40.927
"Come on. It must be just a coincidence."

754
45:41.010 --> 45:42.720
[intense music playing]

755
46:00.572 --> 46:02.699
[timer beeping]

756
46:07.078 --> 46:08.246
Here you go, Chef.

757
46:08.329 --> 46:09.330
Huh?

758
46:09.414 --> 46:11.791
Oh. I was just looking for that.

759
46:11.874 --> 46:13.960
Look at our sweet little Song-yi.

760
46:14.043 --> 46:16.296
Always one step ahead, huh?

761
46:24.345 --> 46:27.432
-Hey, Chef. Can I help you with anything? -Really?

762
46:28.016 --> 46:31.352
Then keep stirring this very slowly so that the sauce doesn't set.

763
46:31.436 --> 46:33.396
-Uh, yes, Chef. -Thank you.

764
46:34.355 --> 46:36.107
-Careful. It's hot. -Okay.

765
46:36.190 --> 46:38.234
You're gonna make a great chef someday.

766
46:38.860 --> 46:40.111
Your dad must be proud.

767
46:40.194 --> 46:42.196
[chef] You're better than your dad already.

768
46:42.280 --> 46:43.823
You're doing better than he is.

769
46:49.370 --> 46:50.705
-[sizzling] -[screams]

770
46:53.833 --> 46:55.460
Jun-ho! Jun-ho!

771
46:56.961 --> 46:58.921
Somebody get some ice and a towel. Quick.

772
46:59.005 --> 47:01.132
Oh, no. The skin's already starting to peel.

773
47:01.215 --> 47:03.968
Hey, this is bad. Take him to the hospital.

774
47:04.052 --> 47:05.345
-Hey, put some ice on his cheek. -Yes.

775
47:05.428 --> 47:07.096
Hey, careful. Careful.

776
47:07.180 --> 47:09.557
[chef 1] Careful. Are you okay? Come on. Right over this way.

777
47:09.641 --> 47:12.018
-Let's go. Be careful. -Okay. We're going to get you out of here.

778
47:15.063 --> 47:16.397
But then,

779
47:16.481 --> 47:18.941
strangely, every time Song-yi went into the kitchen,

780
47:19.692 --> 47:22.195
someone around her would get hurt that day,

781
47:22.278 --> 47:23.946
and really badly too.

782
47:27.784 --> 47:29.160
[crying out]

783
47:30.119 --> 47:32.580
Ah! Ah.

784
47:32.664 --> 47:35.166
[Du-yeong] Knife cuts were the least of it.

785
47:44.759 --> 47:46.010
[gasping]

786
47:46.094 --> 47:47.345
[Du-yeong] Contusions.

787
47:56.896 --> 47:58.314
[both shouting]

788
47:58.981 --> 47:59.982
[chef] Whoa!

789
48:00.942 --> 48:03.319
[both exclaiming]

790
48:03.403 --> 48:04.821
[Du-yeong] Burns.

791
48:09.534 --> 48:12.203
The customer at Table 3 has a serious clam allergy.

792
48:12.286 --> 48:13.329
What should we do?

793
48:13.913 --> 48:15.707
Tell them we'll leave out the clams,

794
48:15.790 --> 48:17.959
but we'll add more mushrooms and vegetables.

795
48:18.042 --> 48:20.211
-And add some extra cream. -Yes, Chef.

796
48:21.754 --> 48:23.297
[grunts]

797
48:26.217 --> 48:27.593
[Du-yeong] Broken bones.

798
48:30.471 --> 48:31.723
[coughing]

799
48:34.434 --> 48:36.394
[coughing continues]

800
48:36.477 --> 48:38.980
[gagging, gasps]

801
48:46.821 --> 48:49.824
[Du-yeong] Even breathing difficulties

802
48:51.200 --> 48:53.161
and full-body paralysis.

803
48:59.292 --> 49:01.043
It couldn't be a coincidence.

804
49:01.127 --> 49:02.462
Every time she walked into the kitchen,

805
49:02.545 --> 49:05.465
-someone would end up walking out injured. -[sighs]

806
49:05.548 --> 49:07.091
[Du-yeong] And the reason for that was…

807
49:07.175 --> 49:09.218
There's a ghost sitting on you.

808
49:10.011 --> 49:12.513
It's perched right on your shoulder.

809
49:17.769 --> 49:19.645
That thing is obsessed with fire.

810
49:20.271 --> 49:24.275
It's even carrying a huge knife, and you didn't know all this time?

811
49:24.358 --> 49:26.110
Stay away from fire.

812
49:26.819 --> 49:29.447
Especially kitchens and places like that.

813
49:29.530 --> 49:33.075
The sight of fire sends it into a total frenzy.

814
49:33.159 --> 49:36.078
When that thing starts swinging its knife around,

815
49:36.162 --> 49:37.747
you won't get hurt.

816
49:37.830 --> 49:39.373
The people around you will.

817
49:39.457 --> 49:41.000
Remember this.

818
49:42.001 --> 49:43.961
Never go near a kitchen.

819
49:44.045 --> 49:45.505
Ever.

820
49:47.632 --> 49:50.092
She didn't really understand what it meant, but it left her uneasy,

821
49:50.176 --> 49:54.430
so she stayed upstairs watching TV instead of going straight into the kitchen.

822
49:54.514 --> 49:57.683
But of all days, the restaurant was completely packed,

823
49:57.767 --> 50:00.436
and the kitchen was shorthanded.

824
50:02.563 --> 50:03.773
Bring me some stock.

825
50:03.856 --> 50:05.066
-Yes, Chef! -Yes, Chef!

826
50:17.161 --> 50:18.162
Stock here!

827
50:18.246 --> 50:21.290
[chef] Three of the eight salads will go out in three minutes.

828
50:21.374 --> 50:24.418
[chef 2] The dill is prepped and ready. Where's the chervil? Chervil!

829
50:24.502 --> 50:27.213
[Seung-hyo] We still need to confirm what mains Tables 5 and 6 ordered.

830
50:27.296 --> 50:29.215
[metal clattering]

831
50:29.298 --> 50:30.925
[whimsical music playing]

832
50:40.560 --> 50:41.727
[sighs]

833
50:44.480 --> 50:46.440
[tense music playing]

834
51:04.375 --> 51:08.462
[intense music playing]

835
51:10.423 --> 51:12.633
[screaming]

836
51:12.717 --> 51:14.010
[groans]

837
51:14.093 --> 51:16.846
[Du-yeong] He was rushed to the hospital, given emergency treatment,

838
51:17.930 --> 51:20.391
then transferred straight to a burn center

839
51:21.976 --> 51:23.769
with third-degree burns on his leg.

840
51:24.353 --> 51:26.647
Part of his muscles and nerves were damaged,

841
51:26.731 --> 51:30.359
so he had surgery, six months of rehabilitation,

842
51:30.985 --> 51:32.486
and he needed a skin graft.

843
51:34.280 --> 51:35.406
And that's when

844
51:35.489 --> 51:38.951
my late brother started walking around with a limp.

845
51:39.035 --> 51:40.494
[sighs]

846
51:41.162 --> 51:42.705
So you have to understand

847
51:43.414 --> 51:47.501
that guilt is why Song-yi took such devoted care of her father.

848
51:47.585 --> 51:49.795
[sighs] Now you understand

849
51:50.755 --> 51:53.549
why she refuses to go into the kitchen.

850
51:53.633 --> 51:55.134
[sighs]

851
51:56.344 --> 51:58.679
[clinking]

852
52:03.059 --> 52:04.685
[mystic inhales sharply]

853
52:04.769 --> 52:06.479
Do you know who can do this job for you?

854
52:06.562 --> 52:07.647
The job?

855
52:08.648 --> 52:09.649
What are you…

856
52:09.732 --> 52:10.983
Gut.

857
52:11.651 --> 52:13.861
Oh, a gut?

858
52:14.612 --> 52:16.989
People can't just drive away ghosts.

859
52:17.073 --> 52:18.824
You need a deity to do it for you.

860
52:19.784 --> 52:21.994
Oh. I see…

861
52:22.787 --> 52:23.996
[inhales deeply]

862
52:25.790 --> 52:27.416
[upbeat music playing]

863
52:29.669 --> 52:30.711
[chuckles]

864
52:32.296 --> 52:34.090
[clicks tongue, inhales deeply] It looks like

865
52:34.173 --> 52:37.093
I will have to call on several deities,

866
52:37.176 --> 52:38.344
but it's not going to be cheap.

867
52:40.096 --> 52:41.347
How much will it be?

868
52:41.430 --> 52:43.099
[inhales deeply] Wait. Let me see…

869
52:46.185 --> 52:49.438
[chanting, in Korean]

870
52:50.731 --> 52:52.900
[chanting continues]

871
52:56.278 --> 52:57.655
[inhales sharply]

872
52:57.738 --> 52:59.991
[exclaiming]

873
53:07.331 --> 53:09.542
[sighs, in English] Fifteen million.

874
53:09.625 --> 53:10.626
What?

875
53:11.627 --> 53:12.712
Fifteen million won?

876
53:14.088 --> 53:15.089
[gasps]

877
53:16.507 --> 53:19.510
I don't even have one million, let alone 15.

878
53:22.471 --> 53:23.931
Excuse me, sir.

879
53:25.016 --> 53:26.559
I'm sorry, but

880
53:27.476 --> 53:30.229
is there any way you could give me a discount?

881
53:34.233 --> 53:35.943
[clearing throat]

882
53:38.362 --> 53:40.573
[chanting, in Korean]

883
53:44.493 --> 53:46.037
[sighs]

884
53:46.912 --> 53:48.914
[exclaiming]

885
53:52.543 --> 53:53.961
-[in English] Oh! -Ten million!

886
53:54.045 --> 53:55.296
[sighs]

887
53:56.338 --> 53:57.423
Ten million?

888
54:00.259 --> 54:01.218
[groans]

889
54:02.511 --> 54:03.512
[sniffs]

890
54:06.098 --> 54:09.101
[chanting, in Korean]

891
54:09.185 --> 54:11.062
F-Five million...

892
54:12.313 --> 54:13.314
[in English] Sir.

893
54:14.065 --> 54:15.691
I'm really sorry, but

894
54:16.776 --> 54:20.196
I honestly can't afford a gut. It's too expensive.

895
54:20.988 --> 54:24.158
Is there anything you can do as a temporary fix?

896
54:25.326 --> 54:28.788
I just need to be able to go into the kitchen until the competition is over.

897
54:30.998 --> 54:34.168
Please, sir. Please, sir, help me.

898
54:36.045 --> 54:37.463
[sighs]

899
54:38.047 --> 54:39.340
It's a temporary talisman.

900
54:40.132 --> 54:42.510
Keep it in your pocket wherever you may go.

901
54:43.094 --> 54:45.596
It should suppress the ghost's energy for a while.

902
54:45.679 --> 54:47.473
[inhales sharply] But remember this.

903
54:48.224 --> 54:49.850
The magical effects

904
54:50.643 --> 54:53.062
of a temporary talisman don't last very long.

905
54:53.145 --> 54:55.523
[inhales sharply] Okay.

906
54:56.023 --> 54:57.024
Thank you, sir.

907
54:58.359 --> 54:59.610
But…

908
55:00.277 --> 55:03.572
how much do you charge for the talisman?

909
55:04.198 --> 55:07.618
W-W-Well, you don't exactly look like you have a lot of money to spare.

910
55:07.701 --> 55:09.620
Just leave a decent fee on your way out.

911
55:10.496 --> 55:11.705
Would that be okay?

912
55:16.794 --> 55:19.255
-Uh… Uh… -Thank you so much. Thank you so much!

913
55:20.131 --> 55:21.423
[sighs]

914
55:21.507 --> 55:23.926
[sighs] Geez.

915
55:24.969 --> 55:27.221
It's hard to make a living these days.

916
55:27.304 --> 55:30.141
FREE MEAL COUPON

917
55:30.850 --> 55:32.059
Free food, huh?

918
55:37.398 --> 55:38.440
[grunts]

919
55:39.275 --> 55:40.943
[rock music playing]

920
55:54.248 --> 55:55.457
[grunts]

921
55:58.627 --> 55:59.795
[grunts]

922
56:14.476 --> 56:18.480
Whenever I saw you climbing here, I used to think

923
56:19.940 --> 56:22.359
she'll have to come back down. [chuckles]

924
56:22.443 --> 56:24.403
Why go through all that trouble? [chuckles]

925
56:25.070 --> 56:26.864
-I don't get it. -[chuckles]

926
56:30.284 --> 56:32.161
But having a goal you can see…

927
56:34.580 --> 56:36.290
is something to be happy about.

928
56:40.586 --> 56:42.046
We're entering too.

929
56:43.714 --> 56:45.299
The Table: 2026.

930
56:45.382 --> 56:48.052
Exception and I, Cha Woo-jin.

931
56:50.888 --> 56:53.390
What? You're not happy?

932
56:54.767 --> 56:56.018
I thought you'd be thrilled.

933
56:56.685 --> 56:58.103
Guess I got carried away. [chuckles]

934
57:05.903 --> 57:06.904
I'm happy.

935
57:08.739 --> 57:09.949
I'm really happy.

936
57:12.618 --> 57:14.078
Thank you, Woo-jin,

937
57:15.788 --> 57:17.122
for joining the show.

938
57:18.540 --> 57:20.751
[pop song playing]

939
57:22.586 --> 57:23.629
Yes, of course.

940
57:23.712 --> 57:26.131
We'll have all the ingredients set up in the pantry, so you can

941
57:26.215 --> 57:28.384
only use what's provided there.

942
57:29.093 --> 57:32.304
-Right. Yes, yes. Then we'll get all that… -That's enough for you guys.

943
57:32.388 --> 57:35.891
-Wednesdays are… -And everything will be laid out.

944
57:35.975 --> 57:37.434
'Cause by the time…

945
57:37.518 --> 57:39.520
Yes, once the main-round contestants are finalized,

946
57:39.603 --> 57:42.439
we'll, uh, let you know the exact schedule.

947
58:04.378 --> 58:05.879
[chuckles]

948
58:13.262 --> 58:14.513
[utensil hits pan]

949
58:16.557 --> 58:18.809
[song continues]

950
58:34.033 --> 58:35.409
TERMINAL 2, ARRIVALS

951
58:42.708 --> 58:45.627
[chattering]

952
59:26.085 --> 59:27.920
CHOI SONG-YI

953
59:41.058 --> 59:44.478
Thank you so much again for making such a difficult decision, Ms. Choi.

954
59:46.230 --> 59:47.606
And…

955
59:48.774 --> 59:50.526
I hope you do really well.

956
59:51.777 --> 59:52.778
I mean it.

957
59:53.612 --> 59:54.822
[chuckles]

958
59:54.905 --> 59:55.906
LIST OF PARTICIPANTS EXCEPTION

959
59:55.989 --> 59:57.157
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026

960
01:00:02.746 --> 01:00:05.666
[upbeat music playing]

961
01:00:35.863 --> 01:00:37.573
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026

962
01:00:39.867 --> 01:00:41.702
[chattering]

963
01:00:43.704 --> 01:00:45.706
[chattering]

964
01:00:48.667 --> 01:00:50.586
[show staff] Chefs who have entered the studio,

965
01:00:50.669 --> 01:00:54.381
please stand behind the sign with your team name on it.

966
01:00:54.965 --> 01:00:58.719
Recording will begin shortly. Please enter promptly.

967
01:00:59.761 --> 01:01:01.054
Once again,

968
01:01:01.638 --> 01:01:04.266
chefs who have entered the studio,

969
01:01:04.349 --> 01:01:07.895
please stand behind the sign with your team name on it.

970
01:01:07.978 --> 01:01:12.107
Recording will begin soon. Please enter promptly.

971
01:01:16.695 --> 01:01:18.155
[contestants laughing]

972
01:01:39.760 --> 01:01:41.678
Recording begins in two minutes.

973
01:01:42.679 --> 01:01:44.264
Studio, standby.

974
01:01:44.348 --> 01:01:47.684
[director] We're rolling in two minutes. Everyone, standby.

975
01:02:38.652 --> 01:02:41.029
[mysterious music playing]

976
01:02:54.668 --> 01:02:56.545
[Woo-jin] I will win no matter what.

977
01:02:56.628 --> 01:02:58.171
I won't lose twice.

978
01:03:07.306 --> 01:03:08.599
[San] Go ahead, Han.

979
01:03:08.682 --> 01:03:10.225
[teenage Han] Dad! Dad!

980
01:03:10.309 --> 01:03:12.227
Take the stairs and get out of here now.

981
01:03:12.311 --> 01:03:13.478
There's no time.

982
01:03:13.562 --> 01:03:15.397
-Hurry. Go! -No, Dad!

983
01:03:16.648 --> 01:03:17.649
I'm going to get help!

984
01:03:17.733 --> 01:03:18.734
Just wait right here!

985
01:03:18.817 --> 01:03:20.235
No. No, Han!

986
01:03:20.819 --> 01:03:23.280
You're going to die too if you stay here.

987
01:03:23.363 --> 01:03:24.781
Do as I say.

988
01:03:24.865 --> 01:03:26.199
Listen to me. Go!

989
01:03:26.283 --> 01:03:28.327
[wood cracking]

990
01:03:29.620 --> 01:03:30.621
[San] Go now!

991
01:03:31.788 --> 01:03:33.665
[panting]

992
01:03:33.749 --> 01:03:34.875
Just go!

993
01:03:35.876 --> 01:03:38.170
-[wood cracking] -[screaming]

994
01:03:38.253 --> 01:03:39.254
[teenage Han] Dad!

995
01:03:39.338 --> 01:03:40.881
Dad!

996
01:03:48.055 --> 01:03:49.056
[winces, gasps]

997
01:03:50.057 --> 01:03:51.058
[sighs]

998
01:03:52.100 --> 01:03:53.101
[sighs]

999
01:03:56.730 --> 01:03:57.773
Dad.

1000
01:03:59.399 --> 01:04:01.151
I'll win no matter what.

1001
01:04:02.861 --> 01:04:04.863
The person who got you killed,

1002
01:04:05.697 --> 01:04:07.240
I'll beat them for you.

1003
01:04:11.078 --> 01:04:12.079
Camera rolling.

1004
01:04:14.206 --> 01:04:16.667
And… cue.

1005
01:04:21.588 --> 01:04:24.508
[pop song playing]

1006
01:04:51.702 --> 01:04:54.538
[Captain Cook] Presenting the theme for round one.

1007
01:04:56.123 --> 01:04:57.124
Right now!

1008
01:04:57.958 --> 01:04:59.251
I didn't think it would be this tough.

1009
01:04:59.835 --> 01:05:01.837
[Captain Cook] You have three hours!

1010
01:05:01.920 --> 01:05:05.006
I plan to challenge the contestants in ways they won't expect.

1011
01:05:05.090 --> 01:05:08.009
[Hae-seon] We have to create something no one's ever seen before.

1012
01:05:08.552 --> 01:05:10.137
[Woo-jin] Do whatever it takes to get it.

1013
01:05:10.220 --> 01:05:13.140
[Song-yi] What exactly are you going to do?

1014
01:05:13.223 --> 01:05:15.183
-[Captain Cook] Three. -[Han] Let's pick up the pace.

1015
01:05:15.267 --> 01:05:18.019
-[Captain Cook] Two. -[Song-yi] Are you even trying to win?

1016
01:05:18.103 --> 01:05:19.521
[Captain Cook] One.

1017
01:05:19.604 --> 01:05:21.815
Please reveal your dishes.

1018
01:05:21.898 --> 01:05:23.525
[Han] Let's win this in style.
